DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  function  ddiirrffdd()  returns the file descriptor associated with the
       directory stream _d_i_r_p.

       This file descriptor is  the  one  used  internally  by  the  directory
       stream.   As a result, it is useful only for functions which do not de‐
       pend on or alter the file position, such as ffssttaatt(2) and ffcchhddiirr(2).  It
       will be automatically closed when cclloosseeddiirr(3) is called.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, ddiirrffdd() returns a file descriptor (a nonnegative  integer).
       On error, -1 is returned, and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

